</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Madsen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Trends in incidence and case fatality rates of acute myocardial infarction in Denmark and Sweden</article-title><source>Heart</source><year>2003</year><volume>89</volume><fpage>507</fpage><lpage>11</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12695453</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/heart.89.5.507</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B5"><citation citation-type="book"><source>Myocardial infarctions in Sweden 1987&#x02013;2002</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>The National Board of Health and Welfare, Centre For Epidemiology</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Peltonen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lundberg</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Huhtasaari</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Asplund</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Marked improvement in survival after acute myocardial infarction in middle-aged men but not in women. The Northern Sweden MONICA study 1985&#x02013;94</article-title><source>J Intern Med</source><year>2000</year><volume>247</volume><fpage>579</fpage><lpage>87</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10809997</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2796.2000.00644.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lundberg</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Wikstrom</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Bostrom</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Asplund</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Exploring sex differences in case fatality in acute my